48
00:02:38.717 --> 00:02:42.008
Interesting! The smaller the house, the lower the bills.

49
00:02:43.317 --> 00:02:47.118
Exactly. I'd love an eco-home with an open-plan design.

50
00:02:48.417 --> 00:02:50.985
The sooner you start saving, the sooner you'll have one.

51
00:02:52.283 --> 00:02:55.107
Grammar focus: Double comparatives.

52
00:02:55.407 --> 00:03:00.007
Use the plus comparative, the plus comparative, to show that two things change together.

53
00:03:00.307 --> 00:03:03.085
For example: The less I own, the happier I feel.

54
00:03:03.385 --> 00:03:06.046
A common phrase is: the sooner, the better.

55
00:03:06.346 --> 00:03:09.135
This structure shows that two things change together.

56
00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:12.884
Now read and listen. Less Space, More Life.

57
00:03:13.184 --> 00:03:16.263
Around the world, more people are choosing smaller homes.

58
00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:21.059
Supporters of minimalism say that the less you own, the freer you are.

59
00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:26.822
Tiny houses and co-living spaces are popular with young people in big cities.

60
00:03:28.117 --> 00:03:32.078
Eco-homes reduce energy bills by using solar power and natural light.

61
00:03:33.383 --> 00:03:36.811
The more we think about how we live, the better choices we can make.

62
